---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { app } from '../config';
---
<Layout title="Ancrate privacy policy" description="How Ancrate reads Apple Notes locally, stores preferences and widget snapshots, and works with independently configured MCP clients.">
  <article class="document wrap privacy-document"><header class="document-header"><p class="eyebrow">Your notes, with care</p><h1>Privacy policy.</h1><p>Updated 12 October 2026.</p></header><div class="prose">
    <p>This policy describes Ancrate’s current macOS app, local MCP server, and this website. {app.supportEmail && <>Contact: <a href={`mailto:${app.supportEmail}`}>{app.supportEmail}</a>.</>}</p>
    <section><h2>Reading Apple Notes</h2><p>Ancrate reads the local Apple Notes database for search and checklist extraction. Database connections are read-only. It has no separate note editor and does not request AppleScript Automation permission.</p><p>Optional slash commands, Markdown typing shortcuts, the selected-text formatting bar and Notes shortcuts use Accessibility permission. Slash and Markdown shortcuts inspect a bounded amount of text around the cursor, remove accepted command tokens or line prefixes through Notes’ native editing actions, and invoke Notes formatting menus. Markdown shortcuts start off and handle typed line prefixes, rather than pasted Markdown or whole documents. The formatting bar also starts off. It reads selection context and up to 128 UTF-16 code units from the selection’s boundaries as temporary local context, then applies enabled native menu actions. It does not copy or replace selected text, and selected text is not logged or transmitted. These integrations do not run in MCP processes, sample mode, or unit-test hosts.</p><p>Folder selections are remembered using local access bookmarks. The main app remains unsandboxed for its cross-app Accessibility integration. Selecting the Notes folder requests narrower access; it is not an OS-enforced restriction on everything the app could access. macOS can still block that store, requiring a broader Full Disk Access fallback. A readable library does not establish that Full Disk Access is disabled.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Preferences and widget data</h2><p>Ancrate stores preferences, selected-folder bookmarks, and excluded note identifiers locally. When widget sharing is enabled, a snapshot in the app’s shared widget container includes selected checklist text, source note titles and identifiers, folders, note dates, and completion state. The widget can continue showing this snapshot while Ancrate is closed.</p><p>Disable <strong>Show my to-dos in the Ancrate widget</strong> to replace the saved snapshot with an empty disabled snapshot. macOS controls when the visible widget refreshes. Sample notes are not published to widgets or MCP clients.</p><p>Folder filters and note exclusions control Ancrate’s to-do views and widget snapshot. They are not access restrictions for MCP, which can read other notes in the library.</p></section>
    <section><h2>MCP clients and other destinations</h2><p>Opening Ancrate does not start an MCP server automatically. A configured MCP client launches a local Ancrate process and can request notes through four read-only tools. The client may send returned content to its AI provider or other services. Review that client’s privacy settings and policy before connecting private notes.</p><p>Ancrate has no built-in analytics or account service and does not send note content to an Ancrate server. Copying, exporting, and opening external links occur when selected by the user. Copied or exported content becomes available to the chosen destination applications. The <strong>Copy support info</strong> button copies only app/build and macOS versions, without note titles, content, or paths.</p></section>
    <section><h2>App updates</h2><p>Ancrate uses Sparkle to check the HTTPS update feed and download signed releases from this website. Automatic checks start off and can be enabled in Ancrate’s Settings. Update requests expose normal network information, such as your IP address and requested URL, to the hosting provider. System-profile reporting is disabled; your notes are not sent when checking for updates. MCP processes and sample mode do not start the updater.</p></section>
    <section><h2>This website and support email</h2><p>This website uses no analytics scripts, advertising trackers, or cookies set by the site. Screenshots use Ancrate’s built-in fictional sample notes. The preview video and images are served from this site without a third-party video player.</p><p>Hosting providers process network information, including IP addresses and request details, to deliver and protect the site.</p><p>If you email support, your email address and the information you include are processed to answer your request. Email service providers process support messages for delivery and storage. Avoid including private note content in a support request.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Questions and updates</h2><p>{app.supportEmail ? <>Contact <a href={`mailto:${app.supportEmail}`}>{app.supportEmail}</a> for privacy questions or requests concerning support correspondence.</> : <>See the <a href="/support/">support page</a> for privacy questions.</>} This page will be updated if the app’s data practices change.</p><p>Apple Notes and macOS are Apple products. Ancrate is an independent companion and is not affiliated with Apple.</p></section>
  </div></article>
</Layout>
